# OneWoW Suite Architecture

Authoritative reference: [`OneWoW/Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`](OneWoW/Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md).

Load the **`onewow-suite-architecture`** skill when authoring lifecycle hooks, new load units, data stores, `ModuleManifest` entries, enable/opt-out, or cross-unit integration.

## Forbidden in orchestrated units

Feature modules, data stores, DevTool sub-modules, and sub-modules must **not** register lifecycle WoW events for init/arming:

- `RegisterEvent("ADDON_LOADED")`
- `RegisterEvent("PLAYER_LOGIN")`
- `RegisterEvent("PLAYER_ENTERING_WORLD")`
- `EventRegistry:RegisterFrameEventAndCallback` on those three events

Only `OneWoW/OneWoW.lua` may register them.

## Required lifecycle patterns

| I need to… | Do this | Do NOT |
|------------|---------|--------|
| Init module DB | `OnAddonLoaded()` on manifest root | `RegisterEvent("ADDON_LOADED")` |
| Arm at login | `OnPlayerLogin()` or `RegisterLoginHandler` | `RegisterEvent("PLAYER_LOGIN")` |
| React to zone / entering world | `OnPlayerEnteringWorld` or `RegisterEnteringWorldHandler` | `RegisterEvent("PLAYER_ENTERING_WORLD")` |
| Hook Blizzard_Foo when it loads | `RegisterAddonLoadedWatcher("Blizzard_Foo", fn)` | Own `ADDON_LOADED` frame |

**Data stores:** `OneWoW:BootStore(ns, { onLogin, onEnteringWorld, ... })` in `Core/Core.lua`.

## PEW vs gameplay events

- **Lifecycle entering-world work** → `BootStore.onEnteringWorld` or `RegisterEnteringWorldHandler` (routes through core dispatch, including mid-session synthetic catch-up).
- **Gameplay events** (`PLAYER_ALIVE`, `BAG_UPDATE`, `ZONE_CHANGED`, `MAIL_SHOW`, …) → direct `RegisterEvent` on a local frame is OK.

## Load units and integration

- **Never call `C_AddOns.LoadAddOn` / `UIParentLoadAddOn` directly** — only `OneWoW/Core/AddonLoader.lua` and `OneWoW/Core/Lifecycle.lua` may. Raw loads bypass soft opt-out, combat deferral, and load tracing. Use `OneWoW:EnsureLoaded` / `WithAddon` / `BringUp`; this applies to Blizzard LoD addons too (e.g. `EnsureLoaded("Blizzard_InspectUI")`).
- No suite-internal `## OptionalDeps` on TOCs — use nil-guards + `OneWoW:EnsureLoaded` / `WithAddon` for explicit user actions only.
- Cross-unit reads: prefer `_API` over `_DB`; route new reads through `DataManager:Query` when available.
- Hub tab order: hub manifest entries require `module` + `tabOrder`; modules register with `order = OneWoW:GetModuleTabOrder("name")` (reads `tabOrder`, not array position).

## Global surface (`ns` is private)

Authoritative reference: [`OneWoW/Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`](OneWoW/Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md) §6.1.

- `local ADDON_NAME, ns = ...` always — never rename the vararg to the addon name
- `ns.db` — internal `DB:Init` handle; not `addon.db`, `ns.addon.db`, or `OneWoW_<Unit>.db`
- `OneWoW_<Unit>_DB` — WoW SV global name (matches TOC `## SavedVariables`)
- `OneWoW_<Unit>_API` — cross-unit **dot-functions** only
- `OneWoW_<Unit> = {}` — hub lifecycle root (colon hooks: `OnAddonLoaded`, `ApplyTheme`, …); not `= ns`, not `local addon = {}` hop
- **`OneWoW`** — core orchestrator singleton (colon API + `OneWoW.*` services); internal files use `ns`; curated publish only in `Core/Facade.lua`
- **Never publish the namespace as a global** — not `OneWoW_<Unit> = ns`, not `_G[ADDON_NAME] = ns` / `_G[addonName] = ns`
- Data stores: `OneWoW:BootStore(ns, { addonName = ADDON_NAME, ... })` — registers `addonName → storeNs` via `Lifecycle.RegisterUnit` (no `_G[addonName] = ns`)
- `_API` uses dot-functions; `OneWoW_GUI` / `OneWoW` use colon-methods (service singletons)

## Pre-commit enforcement

- `no-suite-lifecycle-events` — lifecycle `RegisterEvent` ban
- `no-raw-loadaddon` — raw `LoadAddOn` ban outside the core loader funnel
- `no-suite-internal-optionaldeps` — TOC OptionalDeps policy
- `no-data-manager-bypass` — cross-load-unit SavedVariables access (enforced; hard-fails off the `ALLOWED_FOREIGN_SV` allowlist)
- `no-namespace-publish` — namespace publish / global-surface anti-patterns (§6.1; enforced — see `MIGRATION.md` §3)
